<title>USA: Air Express, AHP in Puerto Rico airfreight.</title>
<headline>Air Express, AHP in Puerto Rico airfreight.</headline>
<dateline>DARIEN, Connecticut 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Express International said it has signed a two-year contract to provide U.S. pharmaceutical group American Home Products with airfreight services between the U.S. and Puerto Rico.</p>
<p>AEI said it will ship raw materials to make pharmaceuticals to AHP plants in Puerto Rico and transport finished product back to the US.</p>
<p>Puerto Rico is a major manufacturing centre for pharmaceuticals, the result of tax benefits now being phased out. Even so, &quot;many airfreight companies continue to report robust traffic activity to and from Puerto Rico,&quot; AEI said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
